node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.env
*.db
# @vscode/test-electron downloads a VS Code build here (extension e2e tests).
.vscode-test/
# The extension's compiled output (tsc + scripts/copy-assets.mjs). It was being
# committed as stale build output; `npm run compile` (run by vscode:prepublish
# and the publish workflow) regenerates it.
vscode-extension/out/
# Packaged extension binaries are build output, not source. Two were committed
# under vscode-extension/ and drifted from the code they were built from; the
# publish workflow builds a fresh .vsix on every release.
*.vsix
# SQLite sidecars + journal are NOT matched by `*.db`, and that gap is exactly
# how two of these got committed: `.freebuff/desktop-v2.db-wal` / `-shm` matched
# no rule at all while the `.db` itself was ignored.
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
.buffconfig.json

# ── Third-party app state (never source) ──────────────────────────────────
# `.freebuff/` is another product's local desktop state directory (its SQLite
# DB, sidecars and project-id). It is runtime detritus of the tool being RUN in
# this directory — never part of Agent-Nuvira — and it must not be committed.
.freebuff/
.codebuff/
.npmrc
# Generated addon builds (agent output during addon-creation tasks)
addon/
# Local issue tracking (not synced to the upstream repo)
issues/

# ── Markdown docs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only the docs PUBLISHED at the website (user-clickable links referring to
# GitHub) are tracked. All other .md files stay local — what appears on
# GitHub is decided per-file. The whitelist below is the published set:
#   * README.md / CHANGELOG.md (repo + npm landing docs)
#   * the 9 docs README.md links to (DESIGN_DECISIONS, ARCHITECTURE,
#     ARCHITECTURE_DIAGRAMS, PRODUCT_STRATEGY, PITCH_DECK, CONTRIBUTING,
#     UPGRADE_ROADMAP, MODELS_EXPLAIN_DEMO)
#   * docs/benchmarks/* (benchmark reports linked from README)
#   * packaging-required READMEs (sdk package, vscode extension + its changelog)
*.md
# Root-level published docs (anchored — a bare `!README.md` would also
# un-ignore tests/README.md, examples/mcp/README.md, etc.)
!/README.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/DESIGN_DECISIONS.md
!/MODELS_EXPLAIN_DEMO.md
!/ARCHITECTURE.md
!/ARCHITECTURE_DIAGRAMS.md
!/PRODUCT_STRATEGY.md
!/PITCH_DECK.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/UPGRADE_ROADMAP.md
!docs/benchmarks/INDEX.md
!docs/benchmarks/m2b-*.md
!docs/GATEWAY.md
!docs/ASSESSMENT_CAPABILITY_GAPS.md
!docs/IMPLEMENTATION_BRIEFS.md
!docs/DASHBOARD_FIRST_PLAN.md
# The false-success / no-resume RCA. It is the only place the *chain* is written
down: write_file's workspace denial, `zip` exiting 0 on `name not matched`, the
lead confirming success from the exit code, `deliverableAuthored: false` written
next to a 5/5 taskPlan, and the resume gate that never loads any of it. Untracked,
the next session re-derives all of that from scratch and re-ships the same bug;
tracked, it is the document each completion change is checked against.
!docs/rca_false_success_and_no_resume.md
!docs/rca_praised_a_broken_app_and_no_op_success.md
# The desktop architecture decision record (Electron shell, ONE GUI-only
# interface, Hermes Desktop as the reference). It settles questions that cost a
# full research pass to answer — renderer choice, single-interface vs panes,
# GUI-only enforcement, and the CLI→GUI parity matrix. Untracked, the next
# session re-litigates a ratified decision and re-does that research; tracked,
# it is the document every desktop change is checked against.
!docs/DESKTOP_APP_PLAN.md
# Machine-derived CLI surface (generated from the live commander tree by
# scripts/generate-commands-surface.mjs, drift-guarded in CI) — a doc that is
# CODE-adjacent build output, not hand-written prose.
!docs/COMMANDS_SURFACE.md
# The curated command reference README.md links to. It MUST be tracked: it was
# silently untracked (caught by `*.md`) while being both the documented home for
# every command AND the target of a README link — a published URL that 404s, and
# a coverage guard that would skip itself on every fresh clone.
!docs/COMMANDS.md
# Inputs to the public documentation build (scripts/build-docs-repo.mjs renders
# them into imdheerajKube/agent-nuvira-documentation). They MUST be tracked: the
# publish workflow checks this repository out and fails with "missing source
# file" when a generator input is absent, so an ignored .md here becomes a
# publish that only breaks in CI.
!docs/PUBLIC_README.md
!docs/USER_MANUAL.md
# The CLI demo cast (docs/demos/nuvira-cli-tour.cast) is a reproducible build
# artifact linked from README.md, and its README documents how to play and
# regenerate it — both must be tracked or the README link 404s.
!docs/demos/README.md
# The full-sweep cast is a LOCAL verification artifact (docs/demos/README.md: "generated
# on demand, not committed") — ~214 KB rebuilt on every `demo:cli:all`. Without this it
# shows up as untracked noise after a regeneration and is one `git add -A` from being
# committed, which the README says it is not.
docs/demos/nuvira-commands-all.cast
# The default skill registry (.agents/skills/) — SKILL.md files are CODE
# artifacts served by the registry, not user docs. Generated + committed via
# scripts/sync-hub-skills.mjs so the configured default registry resolves.
!.agents/skills/**/SKILL.md
!.agents/skills/**/references/*.md
!src/agent-sdk/README.md
!vscode-extension/README.md
!vscode-extension/CHANGELOG.md
# The two guides for the SDK and the editor surface. They are the only pages that
# state what depth each one offers (and, explicitly, what it does not), and both
# are inputs to the public documentation build (scripts/build-docs-repo.mjs) —
# whose publish workflow fails with "missing source file" when an input is absent,
# so an ignored guide here becomes a publish that only breaks in CI. Ignored, they
# also degrade every README/CONTRIBUTING link into a 404 on a fresh clone.
!docs/AGENT_SDK.md
!docs/VSCODE_EXTENSION.md
# The SDK example's README is the only place a consumer learns to copy the
# example out of the repo and run it — a packaging-required doc, not prose.
!examples/sdk/README.md
# Eight source files (read-extract, tool-refusal, messaging-tools, vision-tools,
# neutts-synth, delegation-system, registry, web-dashboard/server) cite this
# tracker by name as the record of the 2026-09-27 false-success incident. It was
# ignored by `*.md` and lost ONCE already; untracked, the next session has to
# re-derive the whole P-list from inline comments. Tracked, every claim in it is
# checkable against its pinned test.
!docs/TOOL_TRUTHFULNESS_TRACKER.md
# The honest capability/stub ledger. Published (not acknowledged) because its
# whole value is that a reader can check each claim against the code; an
# untracked ledger would be a claim no fresh clone can verify.
!docs/CAPABILITY_LEDGER.md
# These three were cited from CODE (`@see …` / "see the G18 entry in …") while
# being ignored by `*.md`, so on a fresh clone those citations pointed at nothing
# — the same failure that lost the tracker above. `scripts/check-doc-citations.mjs`
# now fails on any such citation, and these are published instead of
# acknowledged so the guard needs no exemption for them. Home paths inside were
# scrubbed to `~` (the SECRET_PATTERNS convention in scripts/generate-cli-demo.mjs).
!AGENT_NUVIRA_MAJOR_REVAMP_PLAN.md
!ENTERPRISE_GRADE_TRACKER.md
!NUVIRA_ROUTER_ROADMAP.md

# Book (internal document — not published)
book/

# Editor / IDE workspace settings — machine-local, never project source.
# Without this the release pipeline's `git add -A` swept a stray
# .vscode/extensions.json into the version bump commit.
.vscode/

# macOS
.DS_Store
src/file.ts
src/example.ts
src/fresh.ts
src/forwarded.ts
src/a.ts
src/b.ts

# Live A/B probe results (tests/live/followup-live.test.ts) — local evidence, not source
tests/live/out-*.json

# The agent's default artifact sandbox (`<cwd>/.nuvira/artifacts`, see
# src/tools/modality/shared.ts). Test code that doesn't override
# NUVIRA_ARTIFACTS_DIR writes here, and a release's `git add -A` would sweep it in.
.nuvira/
